{"kind":"assert","text":"Standing ruling after b2cd3c3b. Every gate, control window and\nrun that lasts more than ten minutes starts under `caffeinate -i`.\nThe START act says so. A run that a host sleep broke is a void\nrun. Its END act says \"void: host sleep\" and gives the pmset\nrecord, and it counts as no evidence for or against the head. The\nnext gate at the same head needs no new ruling.\n\nThe sleep of 17:54 to 18:43 also stopped the planner's surveys at\n17:58 and 18:28. My rulings on questions 8, 9 and 10 are in\n97583e65.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}